  "id": "COMPOUND:15029 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 12,13-Dihydroxybakuchiol may interact with CCRF-HSB-2, through a series of target-mediated pathways. The compound is linked to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including 4-Fluorobenzoic acid, tridec-2-ynyl ester and Petroraspailyne B1. These compounds all ultimately target CCRF-HSB-2, indicating a possible pathway of action involving the modulation of microtubule-associated proteins. The presence of multiple targets at different stages of this pathway suggests a complex, possibly redundant, mechanism of action. The scores assigned to these paths are consistent, indicating a plausible, though not yet fully characterized, relationship between 12,13-Dihydroxybakuchiol and CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
